From df9d06771d2e96ecde20a69c064b541a0c2dfb04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:37:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] l2r-local: issue 36: small textures and their import
 trampolines are alwaysinline

An import trampoline (rewriteImport) packs its arguments and calls the
texture's boundary function, which the linked rustc bitcode defines.
Neither carried an inline attribute, so LLVM inlined them into a caller
by its cost model alone: at a call site it judges cold (below 2% of the
caller's entry frequency) only below the cold-call-site threshold, 45,
whatever the threshold of an ordinary site (225, 250 at -O aggressive).
A texture of cost 46 to 250 was inlined at an ordinary call site and
stayed a call at a cold one, with its argument packing. inlinehint does
not help: LLVM applies the cold-site threshold after the hint's.

rewriteImport now names the boundary function in the trampoline's LLVM
attribute "reussir-import-boundary". ImportTrampolineInlinePass (new,
lib/LLVMPass/AllocationSimplication) runs first in the backend's LLVM
pipeline at -O default and -O aggressive, after the texture bitcode is
linked: for each marked trampoline whose boundary function has a body,
when LLVM may inline that call (getAttributeBasedInliningDecision: target
features and attributes compatible, no noinline, not interposable;
isInlineViable), the boundary is not cold, and the call's inline cost
(getInliningCostEstimate) is at most the pipeline's own inline threshold,
both functions get alwaysinline. A texture is then inlined at every call
site exactly when LLVM would inline it at an ordinary one; larger
textures keep the cost model's decision. Both functions stay defined
(external and weak_odr). -O size and -O none are unchanged.
reussir-llvm-opt registers the pass as reussir-import-trampoline-inline.

Tests: llvmpass/import_trampoline_inline.ll (which trampolines are
marked: small, packed, over the threshold, cold, noinline, other target
features, an external boundary; a cold call site inlined with the pass
and kept without it), frontend/ffi_import_inline_cold.rr (a texture of
cost 70 under seven unlikely conditions is inlined at -O default and
-O aggressive; the unpatched rrc keeps the call), and the passthrough
attribute in conversion/trampoline_import_scalar.mlir.
